From cee06f2185f364117919e1bedc91eddf3b9ae3ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:00:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/24] Locked windows scroll at their right edge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Locked, every window let all of the mouse through, so a long Battle
History, Details or a plugin's list could not be scrolled. Details,
Battle History, plugins' windows and the dock now keep a strip 24 px wide
at their right edge, where their scrollbar is, as their input region
(following the window as it is resized), so the wheel there scrolls
them; the rest still lets clicks through. A wheel at the edge of Details
or Battle History that nothing under it would scroll scrolls the panel
under the window's middle. Settings → Meter Settings → "Locked: scroll
at the right edge", on unless turned off. Not while a screenshot tool is
in front.

Locked, a tool window offers no resize at its edges (the backend tells
the pages, meter-windows-locked): the 6 px resize edge took a press in
the strip for a resize and left less of it to scroll.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBQati3x8VviBbpY9juEWf
